{"files":[{"content":"/*\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\n\n    The stencil calculation stops when  ( err >= CONV_THRESHOLD OR  iter > ITER_MAX )\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <time.h>\n#include <sys/time.h>\n\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\n\n// matrix to be solved\ndouble *grid;\n\n// auxiliary matrix\ndouble *new_grid;\n\n// size of each side of the grid\nint size;\nint iter_max_num;\n\n// return the absolute value of a number\ndouble absolute(double num){\n    if(num < 0)\n        return -1.0 * num;\n    return num;\n}\n\n// allocate memory for the grid\nvoid allocate_memory(){\n    size_t cells = (size_t) size * (size_t) size;\n\n    grid = (double *) malloc(cells * sizeof(double));\n    new_grid = (double *) malloc(cells * sizeof(double));\n}\n\n// initialize the grid\nvoid initialize_grid(){\n    int center = size / 2;\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        size_t row = (size_t) i * (size_t) size;\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\n            if ( i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\n                grid[row + (size_t) j] = 100;\n            else\n                grid[row + (size_t) j] = 0;\n            new_grid[row + (size_t) j] = 0.0;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// save the grid in a file\nvoid save_grid(){\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        size_t row = (size_t) i * (size_t) size;\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            fprintf(stdout, \"%lf \", grid[row + (size_t) j]);\n        }\n        fprintf(stdout, \"\\n\");\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\n\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &size);\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &iter_max_num);\n    \n    int hasError = 1;\n    int iter = 0;\n\n    struct timeval time_start;\n    struct timeval time_end;\n\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\n    allocate_memory();\n\n    // set grid initial conditions\n    initialize_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"Jacobi relaxation calculation: %d x %d grid\\n\", size, size);\n\n    // get the start time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_start, NULL);\n\n    // Jacobi iteration\n    // This loop will end if either the maximum change reaches below a set threshold (convergence)\n    // or a fixed number of maximum iterations have completed\n    while ( hasError && iter < iter_max_num ) {\n        double * restrict current = grid;\n        double * restrict next = new_grid;\n\n        hasError = 0;\n        // calculates the Laplace equation to determine each cell's next value\n        #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) reduction(|:hasError)\n        for( int i = 1; i < size-1; i++) {\n            size_t row = (size_t) i * (size_t) size;\n            for(int j = 1; j < size-1; j++) {\n                size_t cell = row + (size_t) j;\n\n                next[cell] = 0.25 * (current[cell+1] + current[cell-1] +\n                                     current[cell-(size_t) size] + current[cell+(size_t) size]);\n\n                double errorCurrent = absolute(next[cell] - current[cell]);\n                if(errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD ){\n                    hasError = 1;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Both buffers have zero boundaries for every grid with an interior. */\n        if (size > 2) {\n            grid = next;\n            new_grid = current;\n        }\n        iter++;\n    }\n\n    // get the end time\n    //gettimeofday(&time_end, NULL);\n\n    //double exec_time = (double) (time_end.tv_sec - time_start.tv_sec) +\n    //                   (double) (time_end.tv_usec - time_start.tv_usec) / 1000000.0;\n\n    //save the final grid in file\n    save_grid();\n\n    //printf(\"\\nKernel executed in %lf seconds with %d iterations.\\n\", exec_time, iter);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/laplace_seq.c"}],"hypothesis":"A contiguous row-major representation improves stencil locality and permits vectorization; ping-ponging the two grids removes the full interior copy sweep, while static row-parallel stencil work uses the available OpenMP cores without changing any cell arithmetic.","notes":"The size guard preserves the sequential behavior for grids with no interior cells; for all grids with interiors, both fixed boundaries are zero before each buffer swap.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace separately allocated rows with contiguous row-major buffers.","Use OpenMP static row decomposition with an integer OR reduction for convergence detection.","Swap Jacobi buffers after each completed stencil instead of copying the interior."]}